### walk_dir_filter

<!-- livebook:{"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","attrs":{"timeout":300,"source":"inl walk_dir_filter (fn : dir_entry -> async.future_pin_send filtering) (walk_dir : walk_dir) : walk_dir =\n    if is_rust () then\n        // async_walkdir wants a Send filter returning Send futures, and native closures hold `Rc`s. The walk polls the\n        // filter on the thread that drives the stream (block_on), so SpiralAssertSend vouches for both. The entry's\n        // future is made before the `async move` block, which then owns it (nothing captured is moved). The filter\n        // closure binds `f` whole: edition 2021 would otherwise capture only the field `f.0` (the non-Send closure).\n        global \"struct SpiralAssertSend<T>(T);\\nunsafe impl<T> Send for SpiralAssertSend<T> {}\\nimpl<T: std::future::Future + Unpin> std::future::Future for SpiralAssertSend<T> {\\n    type Output = T::Output;\\n    fn poll(mut self: std::pin::Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut std::task::Context<'_>) -> std::task::Poll<T::Output> { std::pin::Pin::new(&mut self.0).poll(cx) }\\n}\"\n        inl fn entry =\n            inl future = fn entry\n            async.new_future_move_send fun () =>\n                inl result = future |> async.await_send\n                inl filtering : async_walkdir_filtering =\n                    match result with\n                    | Ignore => !\\($'\"async_walkdir::Filtering::Ignore\"')\n                    | IgnoreDir => !\\($'\"async_walkdir::Filtering::IgnoreDir\"')\n                    | Continue => !\\($'\"async_walkdir::Filtering::Continue\"')\n                filtering\n        !\\\\((walk_dir, fn), $'\"{ let f = SpiralAssertSend($1); async_walkdir::WalkDir::filter($0, move |x| { let f = &f; SpiralAssertSend((f.0)(x)) }) }\"')\n    else\n        inl fn entry = async.new_future_send fun () =>\n            inl result = fn entry |> async.await_send\n            inl filtering : async_walkdir_filtering =\n                match result with\n                | Ignore => !\\($'\"async_walkdir::Filtering::Ignore\"')\n                | IgnoreDir => !\\($'\"async_walkdir::Filtering::IgnoreDir\"')\n                | Continue => !\\($'\"async_walkdir::Filtering::Continue\"')\n            filtering\n        !\\\\((walk_dir, fn), $'\"async_walkdir::WalkDir::filter($0, move |x| $1(x))\"')","print_code":false},"livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl walk_dir_filter (fn : dir_entry -> async.future_pin_send filtering) (walk_dir : walk_dir) : walk_dir =
      if is_rust () then
          // async_walkdir wants a Send filter returning Send futures, and native closures hold `Rc`s. The walk polls the
          // filter on the thread that drives the stream (block_on), so SpiralAssertSend vouches for both. The entry's
          // future is made before the `async move` block, which then owns it (nothing captured is moved). The filter
          // closure binds `f` whole: edition 2021 would otherwise capture only the field `f.0` (the non-Send closure).
          global "struct SpiralAssertSend<T>(T);\nunsafe impl<T> Send for SpiralAssertSend<T> {}\nimpl<T: std::future::Future + Unpin> std::future::Future for SpiralAssertSend<T> {\n    type Output = T::Output;\n    fn poll(mut self: std::pin::Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut std::task::Context<'_>) -> std::task::Poll<T::Output> { std::pin::Pin::new(&mut self.0).poll(cx) }\n}"
          inl fn entry =
              inl future = fn entry
              async.new_future_move_send fun () =>
                  inl result = future |> async.await_send
                  inl filtering : async_walkdir_filtering =
                      match result with
                      | Ignore => !\($'"async_walkdir::Filtering::Ignore"')
                      | IgnoreDir => !\($'"async_walkdir::Filtering::IgnoreDir"')
                      | Continue => !\($'"async_walkdir::Filtering::Continue"')
                  filtering
          !\\((walk_dir, fn), $'"{ let f = SpiralAssertSend($1); async_walkdir::WalkDir::filter($0, move |x| { let f = &f; SpiralAssertSend((f.0)(x)) }) }"')
      else
          inl fn entry = async.new_future_send fun () =>
              inl result = fn entry |> async.await_send
              inl filtering : async_walkdir_filtering =
                  match result with
                  | Ignore => !\($'"async_walkdir::Filtering::Ignore"')
                  | IgnoreDir => !\($'"async_walkdir::Filtering::IgnoreDir"')
                  | Continue => !\($'"async_walkdir::Filtering::Continue"')
              filtering
          !\\((walk_dir, fn), $'"async_walkdir::WalkDir::filter($0, move |x| $1(x))"')
  """,
  timeout: 300_000
)
```

